      "writtenOn": "2023-11-02T10:41:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have a question.\n\nThe spec says that the user shall be notified of the encryption setup failure.\nCurrently, there is no notification in AOSP structure.\n\nHowever, if the codes I suggested are applied, if encryption fail occurs, pairing popup for new pairing will occur. Isn\u0027t this rather matched to the spec?\n\nOf course, I limited key missing case. However, this can be modified.",
      "parentUuid": "cef5adfe_0aa4b523",
      "revId": "fb47c372d574467e723ffe8dde1565c754300934",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ccc73591_550d3e68",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-26T22:08:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e link is maintained and data can be transmitted\nThe proposed change does not match the intention to prevent data exchange.\nMaintaining the link is fine as long as the data transmission is not allowed. Link is needed to be maintained for any possible repairing attempt.",
      "revId": "fb47c372d574467e723ffe8dde1565c754300934",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2cc7d24a_b2b96877",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120880
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-30T08:30:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because apps have paired through createBond, it will send the data assuming that it is encrypted.\nIn general, apps do not always check whether the link is bonded or not when sending data.\n\nIf the encryption is released by key missing and the data is not transmitted due to it, the app is not known why it cannot communicate data without a callback related to success of encryption.\nTherefore, I think that BT stack have to send a callback related to enctyption success for the implementation you talked about.\nDo you think this structure is better?",
      "parentUuid": "ccc73591_550d3e68",
      "revId": "fb47c372d574467e723ffe8dde1565c754300934",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
